					"__type" : "textStyle"
				},
				"string" : "---\n\n# Phase 4 — Malicious packages (OSSF, via OSV)\n\nMalicious-package reports live **inline** in OSV query results — they're distinguished by a `MAL-*` id and/or a `database_specific.malicious-packages-origins` marker. {{gtClass:Gt4SecurityVulnerability}} has `isMalicious` and `maliciousOrigins`; {{gtClass:Gt4SecurityVulnerabilityGroup}} has type-preserving `malicious` / `benign` filters.\n\n## 20. Look up a known MAL- record directly\n\n`MAL-2022-4301` is an npm typosquat of `libidn2` catalogued by OSSF. Inspect the result — the **Summary** view shows `Malicious?: YES`, and a new **Malicious origins** tab lists the reporter metadata."
			},
