				"paragraphStyle" : {
					"__type" : "textStyle"
				},
				"string" : "---\n\n# Data coverage additions: KEV, CWE, Severity, Alias, Credits\n\nEvery structured field on a {{gtClass:Gt4SecurityVulnerability}} is now a first-class domain object or group. Inspect a vuln and you'll see tabs for **CISA KEV** (if applicable), **CWEs**, **Aliases**, **References**, **Affected**, **Credits**, **CVSS vector**. The Raw view exposes all ivars as typed groups — no `an Array [N items] (a Dictionary(...))` dead ends.\n\n## 23. CISA KEV: actively exploited flag\n\nCVE-2024-23222 is in the CISA Known Exploited Vulnerabilities catalog. Inspect the result — the **Summary** shows `In CISA KEV?: YES — actively exploited`, and a dedicated **CISA KEV** tab shows when it was added, the federal patch deadline, and the vulnerability name."
			},
